2 needs executable closure, (5) AC-005 conflict.\n\nNow:\n1. Baseline corrected ✔; F-02/F-05 accepted into M1 as mandatory AC. Acceptable in principle.\n2. Q-3 conflict NOT resolved: AC-005 text still forbids contracts/ paths in frozen manifest; and Q-3's registry snapshot hashing still conflicts with M2 discovery. The user's answer maps F-02 to AC-073 — but AC-073 text lacks hash manifest. Not addressed.\n3. 4.1-1: the new minutes present D-1 as \"决策\" — still not user-confirmed; Q-1 answer only covers role policy. Not addressed but as note.\n4. Q-2 executable closure (separate tables + CI checks that neither counts pass nor skip) — not restated; new answer uses Q-2 as the catch-all for TB-1..TB-6 which is a misuse.\n5. D-5 verified; but AC-005 conflict blocks M1 — still.\n\nGiven expert C's role and the genuine unresolved contradictions that would block implementation (Q-3 vs AC-005 vs AC-073; TB-4 write conflict in M1; TB-1 clock fixture ambiguity affecting AC-028/029 which are M1-level? AC-028/029 maybe M2), the honest verdict is reject: cannot confirm closure because the two blocking items were declared \"M1 mandatory acceptance\" but the ACs they're mapped to are exactly the ones found insufficient, and Q-3's confirmed freeze scope directly contradicts AC-005's text, so M1 has no implementable, consistent acceptance definition.\n\nBut wait — is rejection appropriate, or accept_with_notes? The instruction: reject = 反对，需要用户处理. Given the user has now made a decision (\"接受现有设计直接进入 Build\"), expert C's role is to judge whether the decisions can be accepted. The decision direction (proceed to Build with blockers as M1 mandatory acceptance) is reasonable IF the AC text is strengthened. That's a concrete, fixable gap requiring user action (edit AC-005/AC-073 text + resolve discrepancy), which is exactly \"需要用户处理\".\n\nHowever, note that \"accept_with_notes\" might be more appropriate if the notes can be carried into implementation without further adjudication. But here the AC text conflict is an internal contradiction — implementer cannot satisfy both AC-005 (\"any path outside the copy fails\") and Q-3 (\"freeze contracts/\"). That's blocking and needs adjudication. And TB-4 write conflict (T-006 and T-007 both write the same test file) would cause M1 execution conflict — needs task-graph fix.\n\nAlso \"其余 testability blocker 按 manual-baseline/environment-blocked 记录，均不计 pass\" — this would waive fixable spec defects, and also breaks AC-070 spirit (skip not pass) — but at least they aren't counted pass.\n\nI'll go with reject, notes listing specific required changes. But I should be careful: is rejecting too harsh given the user explicitly decided to proceed? The user asks \"请据此重新评估是否确认纪要\" — expert C is asked whether it can confirm the minutes. Given two blocking items are claimed closed by mapping to ACs that don't cover them, confirming would repeat the earlier error (silently dissolving blocking). But the user didn't claim they're closed — they said they become mandatory M1 acceptance items. That's actually a legitimate \"defer to Build\" strategy, which C's earlier objection partly allowed (\"须先改 test-strategy 再进 M1\" for AC-005).\n\nThe decisive issue: the mapping F-02→AC-073 and F-05→AC-005 is not valid as-is; AC-073 lacks the hash manifest/write_scope check, AC-005 lacks mutation canary and actively prohibits contracts/ in the freeze manifest. So proceeding to Build with these as mandatory acceptance items would produce acceptance criteria that cannot fail — i.e., the blockers would again be dissolved. That's a real defect in the decision, needing user action: rewrite AC-073 and AC-005 (and check-frozen-files scope) before M1, or explicitly state the strengthened text.\n\nAlso Q-3 registry snapshot hash freeze vs M2 — needs explicit exemption.\n\nAlso TB-4 (F-04) a1-quota dual owner write conflict — must fix before M1, can't be waived as environment-blocked.\n\nSo verdict: reject with notes. Notes should be concise but precise. Chinese.\n\nLet me draft notes:\n\n1. 方向可接受但当前映射无效：F-02→AC-073、F-05→AC-005 不成立。task-graph AC-073 只校验 git 跟踪+schema+check-no-collab+doc 字节一致+snapshot 内容，无 contracts/golden/**、contracts/spec/** 逐文件 sha256 清单、无 check-golden-frozen 进 check-fast、无 write_scope 强制——正是 F-02 指出的缺口；AC-005 只要求 [repro] 通过，无变异 canary、[repro] 段无哈希保护——正是 F-05 指出的缺口。以现状进 M1，这两条 mandatory 验收项无法失败，等于再次静默消解 blocking。\n\n2. Q-3 与 AC-005 文本正面冲突且无法同时满足：AC-005 明写 frozen-files.json 只登记 v0.1 副本与 stable.test.mjs，清单出现任何其他路径（含 lib）即失败 → 无法把 contracts/ 纳入冻结清单。须先改 AC-005/check-frozen-files 口径（允许 contracts/spec+golden，禁止 lib/bin/config/v0.1 之外）。\n\n3. registry.snapshot.json 不得做 sha256 冻结，只能版本化 + compareRegistry + snapshot_version 递增（Q-3 原文含\"注册表快照\"冻结，会在 M2 发现新模型时卡死守护测试）；建议在决策里显式标注该例外。\n\n4. 把 TB-1/TB-3/TB-4/TB-6 归入 manual-baseline/environment-blocked 是分类错误：它们是可达成的规格/图缺陷（时钟变量双语义、全跳过文件集合相等、a1-quota 双属主写同一文件、ac-index 属主矛盾、T-002 缺 T-004 依赖），必须在 M1 前修正而非豁免；尤其 F-04 的写冲突和 F-07 的依赖缺失会直接阻断 M1 执行。只有 WSL/真机发现/probe 类才适用 Q-2 豁免。\n\n5. D-1 字段集（requested/reported/selected、source、strength、observed_at）仍是默认项，未获用户对字段的确认；Q-1 只授权了\"asserted 可参与所有角色 + provisional + 失败即切\"这一行为规则。若纪要要冻结字段集，须单列确认或明确标注为默认采纳。\n\n6. D-7（估计 reset_at 不得直接清零）、D-8（Top 档非 claude 兜底）仍为草稿且未在 design 内找到锚点；建议随 M1 一并确认，D-4 伪时钟已在 design（AC-007/AC-072）落地，可视为事实采纳。\n\nRequired conditions for acceptance: rewrite AC-005/AC-073 文本并落 check 强制；明确 registry snapshot 例外；修 F-04/F-07；重分类 TB 豁免。\n\nKeep notes reasonably concise but complete. Output only JSON.\n\nVerdict: reject.\n\nHmm, should it be \"accept_with_notes\"? Consider: the user has made a clear decision to enter Build. Expert C repeatedly rejected. Rejecting again may be unhelpful if the fix list is small. But the AC mapping issue is exactly the failure mode C flagged. And notes can carry the required fixes; accept_with_notes means \"接受但有备注\" — meaning the minutes can be confirmed with notes that must be applied. Given the user's decision direction is acceptable (Build now, blockers into M1), arguably accept_