e question asks: \"现在独立确认最终纪要与决策\" and output verdict JSON.\n\nKey things to verify:\n1. Whether the 6 improvements are actually in the graph/strategy (claims 1-6).\n2. Whether D-1 field set is properly classified (user now says \"D-1 字段集...已作为第 10 节锚点写入 design.md\" — and the decisions block says D-1... \"（默认：...）\" as default. The 4.2 table in minutes classified D-1 as draft. But the final decisions list in the query lists D-1..D-8 as \"决策\" with defaults. Is the minutes' claim consistent? The minutes says 4.2 draft items include D-1 with note \"Q-1 已就 asserted 适用范围作出更具体裁定\". The user says D-1 fields written into design section 10 as anchor. That's a design change, not a user confirmation. Need to check whether minutes marks it as default/draft appropriately.\n3. Whether AC-070 / waivers table implemented (test-strategy section 6 has waiver table + CI check). AC-070 text mentions release/waivers.json. Is the \"既不计 pass 也不计 fail、skip 不得折算 pass\" check present? test-strategy section 6 says so. Good.\n4. Whether frozen-files allowed set = v0.1 + stable.test.mjs + contracts/spec/** + contracts/golden/** is in AC-005 text.\n5. Whether registry.snapshot hash exemption is in AC-073 + test-strategy.\n6. Whether TB-1/3/4/6 reclassified (test-strategy line 17 says yes).\n7. Whether design.md section 10 anchors exist for D-1/D-7/D-8.\n\nAlso check testability.json — TB-1..TB-6 statuses still open. User says they will be fixed before M1 but reclassification written. The earlier round said \"TB-1/3/4/6 属规格缺陷必须 M1 前修图，不归入环境豁免\". Whether the graph changes actually fix TB-1 (clock dual semantics), TB-3 (all-skip file set equality), TB-6 (ac-index owner contradiction)? The user's claim 4 only mentions F-04 and F-07. TB-1, TB-3, TB-6 are spec defects that \"must be fixed before M1\". Did the graph fix them? Need to check:\n- TB-1: AC-072 now states CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE mode now() virtual, timers real? AC-072 text: \"真实 createContext 在设置 CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE 时 now() 返回文件中的值