lden-frozen is included automatically. Good. check-write-scope in T-004 outputs. Good.\n\n2. F-05 → AC-005: verified. Mutation canary for each defect; [repro] sha256 in defects.json; [repro]/[fixed] separated; check-frozen-files in check-fast. Note: \"变异 canary\" uses \"已修复的 v0.1 变体\" — but wait, v0.1 is the buggy copy; \"已修复的 v0.1 变体\" means a variant where the bug is fixed. Reasonable.\n\n3. Registry snapshot exemption: verified in AC-073 and test-strategy item 3. But AC-005 still includes \"contracts/spec/**、contracts/golden/** 的 sha256\" — registry.snapshot.json is in contracts/ root, not spec/golden, so no conflict. Good.\n\n4. Q-3 conflict with design.md §5/§0: AC-005 graph rewritten but design.md line 28/127 unchanged, still says only v0.1 + stable.test.mjs allowed. This means the \"design\" still contradicts AC-005. The user only modified graph + strategy. Does that matter? The minutes says Q-3's confirmed scope; the graph AC-005 now aligns with Q-3. But the design doc still says the opposite, and design.md is part of the blueprint that builders read. However, the plan says \"改的是图与策略\" and accepts that design wasn't re-reviewed. Still, \"single source of truth\" is contracts/ at runtime; design.md is historical. But an implementer reading design.md §5 would implement the wrong allowed set. The blueprint is build input; contradictions in design are a risk. Is it blocking for acceptance of the minutes? The minutes claims decisions, not that every doc is consistent. But my prior rejection specifically said \"按第 2 点改写 Q-3 冻结口径并与 design.md:28、design.md:126-127 对齐\". The user responded by rewriting AC-005 (graph) and test-strategy but NOT design.md:28/126-127. Hmm — that was a prior explicit requirement (\"须同步改写 AC-005 与 check-frozen-files 的允许集合...\"). They did rewrite AC-005 and check-frozen-files is presumably in scripts (nonexistent yet, T-002 output). design.md line 127 still has old rule, and T-002 output includes check-frozen-files.mjs; the graph's AC-005 governs. So the build-time contract (AC + task graph) is aligned; design prose is stale. Since ACs are authoritative for gates, maybe acceptable with note.\n\n5. D-1 field set: Q-1 only authorized behavior; user's latest answer says fields \"已作为第 10 节锚点写入 design.md\". design.md §10.1 does contain the fields. Is that \"user confirmed\"? The decisions list presents D-1 with \"（默认：...）\" — implying default adoption, not user confirmation. The minutes 4.2 table marks D-1 as draft with note. But the final \"决策\" section lists D-1..D-8 without marking draft/confirmed. Ambiguity. The query's minutes say 4.2 all default items are drafts, and 4.1 only Q-1..Q-5. The user's Q-6/Q-7 answers added more: \"六条已按可判据改造完成...6) D-1 字段集、D-7 估计刷新、D-8 Top 档兜底已作为第 10 节锚点写入 design.md\". This is a user action, arguably confirming those anchors? It says they've been written, not that they're approved. Hmm.\n\nThe instruction: \"请判断是否可以接受这些决策\" — the decisions are D-1..D-8. As expert C, I need to judge whether I accept them.\n\nMy stance historically: D-2/D-4 already in design (AC-007/AC-072) — accept by fact. D-3 contracts/ single source — aligns with Q-3 and AC-073 — acceptable. D-5 M1 independent — accept. D-6 split integration/E2E — accept. D-1 fields — behavior rule confirmed, field set is a reasonable implementation of it, now anchored in design §10.1; Q-1 confirmed behavior; D-1's \"AgentLine 不再重复硬判\" is the user's original premise in the topic (\"身份与可用性应当由 CLIWorker 统一处理\") — actually the user's own Q1 statement says \"身份与可用性应当由 CLIWorker 统一处理\". So D-1's core is user's own framing. Fine. D-7 estimated reset_at — sound, now anchored §10.2. D-8 Top tier non-claude fallback — sound, anchored §10.3.\n\nSo decisions per se are acceptable. The issue is the claim that all six items are \"改造完成\" and F-04 residual.\n\nLet me check the minutes-final.md to see whether it's updated to reflect Q-6/Q-7 or still the stale version. If the final minutes file still says only Q-1..Q-5 and \"4 blocking\", that's a problem because the user asks to confirm 最终纪要. Let me read minutes-final.md and decisions.json.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b631861d76b2a08c72bb6c9ff9ad","_messageId":"01a1b63231c174398dcd8d0e3fb40249","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b631861d76b2a08c72bb6c9ff9ad","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b63231c174398dcd8d0e3fb40249","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b63231c174398dcd8d0e3fb40249","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b632-31c1-7439-8dcd-8d10d326b4cb","traceparent":"00-f1d3e59acc86b4a7b6caa1170d79b2ee-5201346c6ef2d0a0-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b631-833e-7cce-99be-733d57cd5e95,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b631861d76b2a08c72bb6c9ff9ad"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T13:28:40.356Z"}
