{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b632-6cbb-7c33-be40-84c25cedf248","session_id":"01a1b631-833e-7cce-99be-733d57cd5e95","message":{"id":"01a1b6326cba7a3f8b7e947351d3062f","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important: decisions.json marks D-1..D-8 all \"status: default_adopted\" and \"confirmed_by_user kind: default\". The minutes (both file and query) classify D-1..D-8 as 草稿 (4.2), saying user didn't confirm. So there's a metadata inconsistency between minutes and decisions.json, but the minutes is the authoritative record per the query. The decisions JSON records default adoption as \"confirmed_by_user\" with kind default — arguably per the system's convention, default adoption counts as user confirmation. The minutes says \"默认采纳即构成用户确认\" for Q-1..Q-5, yet says D-1..D-8 not confirmed. But decisions.json claims defaults were adopted by user at 13:20:06. Hmm.\n\nThe query's final decision list D-1..D-8 appears as formal \"决策\" (not marked draft), each with default. So the Studio system has treated these as adopted defaults. In previous rounds, expert C objected that D-1 fields etc. were drafts. The user then wrote them into design.md §10 as anchors. So arguably user action confirmed them.\n\nNow, what is the actual question: \"你是本次 Studio 讨论的专家 C（expert_c），现在独立确认最终纪要与决策。\" Judge whether to accept. Output verdict JSON.\n\nGiven my prior stance as expert C, the key unresolved items are:\n1. TB-1 (clock env var dual semantics) — not fixed in AC-061/AC-072; test-strategy even says \"须写明两种时钟模式不可混用\" (still an open obligation). Marked as \"must fix before M1\" so acceptable as a pre-M1 gate, but the minutes' claim \"六条已按可判据改造完成\" is false for TB-1. However, does the minutes claim that? The query's Q-7 answer does. The minutes revision record includes the user's answer verbatim. If I accept, I should note these residual items must be resolved before M1; but if they're not in the graph, M1 will start with them unfixed.\n\n2. TB-3 (all-skip) — not fixed. AC-001 unchanged. This will break ubuntu/macos full runs. It's a real blocker for M1 CI (M1 includes T-001 runner). The review said \"F-03 会让 ubuntu/macos 完整运行必然失败\" and \"必须在 M1 前修图\". Not fixed. That's significant: M1's acceptance includes AC-001 across 3 OS. Without fixing, M1 cannot pass.\n\n3. TB-6 (ac-index owner) — design.md §0 line 18 still says all contracts/spec files written by T-004, while §4 line 107 says ac-index by T-001. Graph: T-001. The contradiction persists in design text. TB-6 was explicitly \"须统一 §0/§4/任务图三处表述\". Not done.\n\n4. TB-4 (a1-quota dual owner) — write_scope conflict removed but outputs still assign [fixed] sections to T-006/T-007 while a1-quota not in their write_scope; design §5 line 143 still says T-006/T-007 dual owner; defects.json single owner_task; no per-owner subsection validation. So the underlying misjudgment risk remains, plus new deadlock. Not fixed.\n\n5. TB-5 (defects repro hash) — fixed in AC-005.\n\n6. TB-2 (golden oracle) — fixed in AC-073.\n\nSo 2 of 6 testability blockers resolved; 4 remain, and my prior accept condition said \"把 TB 豁免重新分类\" — which was done — but also \"修好 F-04/F-07 的图冲突\". F-07 fixed; F-04 partially (write conflict removed but outputs/owner still contradictory). TB-1/TB-3/TB-6 were required to be fixed pre-M1, not necessarily pre-accept. The prior minimum accept condition didn't require fixing TB-1/TB-3/TB-6, only reclassifying them (not as environment waivers). The user did that. So strictly by my stated minimum conditions, accept might be warranted, with notes that TB-1/3/6 + F-04 residual must be M1 preconditions.\n\nBut wait — my prior round said: \"这四项是文本与图内可完成的修改，不需要重跑蓝图评审。\" The four: (1) strengthened text AC-005/AC-073/test-strategy, (2) registry exemption, (3) fix F-04/F-07 graph conflicts, (4) reclassify TB waivers. Item 3 is only half done (F-07 done, F-04 partially). Item 1 done. Item 2 done. Item 4 done.\n\nDoes partial F-04 justify reject? The a1-quota conflict: with write_scope removed from T-006/T-007, and outputs still claiming they produce [fixed] for a1-quota, plus design §5 saying dual owner, there is an inconsistency that will block delivery. It's a concrete, checkable defect: check-write-scope (AC-073) would fail any change by T-006/T-007 to a1-quota.test.mjs outside their write_scope. And milestone-gate would accept one half. That's exactly F-04's harm, still present.\n\nHmm, but maybe the intent: T-002 is now the single owner of a1-quota.test.mjs file, and T-006/T-007 provide the assertions to T-002? No, that's not how tasks work; they'd have to write it. The outputs say \"defects/a1-quota 的预测部分 [fixed]\" — a task output. If they can't write it, they can't produce it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe T-002's write_scope covers the whole file and T-006/T-007 \"contribute\" content via separate files? Not stated.\n\nSo: accept_with_notes vs reject. The instruction: reject means \"反对，需要用户处理\"; accept_with_notes means \"接受但有备注\". The decisions themselves (D-1..D-8) — do I oppose them? No, they're sound and now anchored. The minutes' factual claims are mostly verified; but the claim \"六条已按可判据改造完成\" is overstated, and 4 of 6 TB remain open, with TB-3 guaranteed to break M1 CI, TB-4 creating a write_scope deadlock, TB-6 design contradiction. If I accept the decisions but note that M1 must not start until these are fixed, that's accept_with_notes. But is that enough? The minutes claims the six are done; if I accept, the record would falsely imply closure — which is what I've rejected twice (\"不能第三次把 blocking 静默消解\"). The pattern matters: I rejected twice for exactly \"声称已处置但实际未闭环\". Now 2 of 4 relevant F items fixed, but F-04 half-fixed and TB-1/3/6 untouched while the user asserts \"六条已按可判据改造完成\". That's a factual misstatement. So reject again? The user may be frustrated, but integrity requires accuracy.\n\nLet me carefully verify whether TB-1/TB-3/TB-6 might have been addressed elsewhere (acceptance-matrix.md, interfaces.md, task-graph beyond AC text). TB-6: design §0 line 18 vs §4 line 107. The graph T-001 owns ac-index; T-004 doesn't. Design §0 is the only contradiction. Perhaps design §0 line 18 phrase \"这些文件\" refers to registry snapshot + spec + golden collectively but §4 clarifies exception. Still contradictory text. TB-6's requirement was to unify three places; not unified.\n\nTB-1: check interfaces.md §3? Maybe interfaces has clarifications. Let me grep interfaces.md for CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE and health semantics.\n\nTB-3: grep interfaces/design for \"已加载\" or \"全跳过\".\n\nAlso check AC-070/waiver table implementation: test-strategy item 6, AC-070 mentions release/waivers.json but not manual-baseline/environment-blocked tables. Q-2 confirmed \"同时引入 manual-baseline 和 environment-blocked...豁免单独列出\". Does the graph implement both states? AC-070 still only mentions waivers for real-smoke. Q-2's decision may be unimplemented in the graph: environment-blocked (for WSL etc.) and manual-baseline not present. test-strategy item 5 says manual-baseline/environment-blocked only for real environment limits, item 6 says waiver table; but AC-070 text doesn't mention them. Hmm, AC-070 references \"release/waivers.json\" only. The Q-2 confirmed decision #2 says introduce both. Is there an AC implementing manual-baseline/environment-blocked? Let me grep task-graph for \"manual-baseline\" and \"environment-blocked\".\n\nLet me grep across blueprint files.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b631861d76b2a08c72bb6c9ff9ad","_messageId":"01a1b6326cba7a3f8b7e947351d3062f","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b631861d76b2a08c72bb6c9ff9ad","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6326cba7a3f8b7e947351d3062f","codebuddy.ai/llmM